From 9656cb372ef56dd53d0365c85c29dc0ee812e40f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Charles Ci-Jyun Wu <dminus@andestech.com>
Date: Thu, 28 Sep 2023 16:42:18 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 013/168] riscv: dts: andes: add dma-noncoherent property to
 support noncoherent device

Under CONFIG_RISCV, which selects ARCH_DMA_DEFAULT_COHERENT, all devices
are assumed to be DMA-coherent by default.

commit c00a60d6f4a14 ("of: address: always use dma_default_coherent
for default coherency")

For noncoherent devices that require noncoherent DMA, 'dma-noncoherent'
should be added to their device nodes.

Signed-off-by: Charles Ci-Jyun Wu <dminus@andestech.com>
---
 arch/riscv/boot/dts/andes/a25_c1_d_dsp_noncoherent_ae350.dts | 5 +++++
 .../boot/dts/andes/a27l2_c1_d_dsp_noncoherent_ae350.dts      | 5 +++++
 arch/riscv/boot/dts/andes/a45_c1_d_dsp_noncoherent_ae350.dts | 5 +++++
